.TH EUCLID-CLI-EQS-GET-MESSAGE-COUNT 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eqs-get-message-count \- return a queue's message counters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli eqs get-message-count
.BR \-\-ern | \-e
.I ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Returns a queue's message counters, such as the total number of
messages, the number currently invisible (in flight to a receiver), and
the number delayed (not yet visible due to the queue's delivery delay).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-ern " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the queue. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The queue's message counters are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no queue
with that ERN exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eqs get-message-count \e
    --ern ern:euclid:queues:eu-central-1:000000000000:queue:orders
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eqs (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eqs-get-queue-metadata (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
